// Type-checks the test-support layer: the dev harness, the in-memory DOM and
// other doubles, and the fixtures.
//
// The tier test files themselves are deliberately not here. They hand shim
// nodes (`DomElement`) to production functions that expect real `Element`s, and
// the two are unassignable by construction -- a real `Element` has ~150 more
// members -- so covering them means a cast at every boundary (73 errors
// measured on 2026-10-09). They are exercised at runtime instead, where a stale
// field reference mostly fails an assertion loudly. This layer is the one where
// a stale field is silent: a fixture or harness object typed `TweetData` that
// no longer matches the type drifts without any test touching it.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": [
    "src/env.d.ts",
    "dev/**/*.ts",
    "tests/env/**/*.ts",
    "tests/fixtures/**/*.ts"
  ]
}
